# SSoT Path: gcs-core-governance/.gitignore
#
# DERIVED FILE — do not hand-edit the canonical block below.
#
# Lines 45-244 of this file are a BYTE-IDENTICAL copy of gct-repo-template-standard/.gitignore,
#   sha256 049729bcdf52ccdb6bbdba1b8a1a0aa8170119e98a5683ff822b0f882ca9aed0
# That template states it "should be the base for all new repositories". This repo is the
# governance SSoT for exactly that kind of config, so it adopts the canonical template rather
# than minting a bespoke variant (#307 review, HIGH 3).
#
# To re-sync: replace EXACTLY lines 45-244 (not through the ─── rule or the marker below), then
# re-apply this header and the addendum, then re-check the sha256 above. Do NOT `cp` the template
# over this file wholesale — that deletes this header.
#
# TWO TRAPS, both real today:
#
# 1. SEVERAL PATTERNS APPEAR TWICE, and `git check-ignore -v` reports only the LAST match. `.env`
#    is at :165 AND :203; likewise dist/, build/, *.log, venv/, env/, and .venv vs .venv/. Delete
#    the :203 `.env` believing you removed the rule and it stays ignored via :165 — which reads as
#    a broken .gitignore. Being fixed upstream in gct-repo-template-standard#45 (de-duplication).
#
# 2. THE REAL HAZARD IS THE NEXT reference-libraries/ SYNC, not additions to this file. Directory
#    patterns here are unanchored, so of 14 plausible upstream path shapes, 12 would match --
#    lib/ build/ target/ var/ dist/ env/ instance/ htmlcov/ *.log MANIFEST override.tf *.tfvars.
#    Vendored content matching any of them vanishes from `git status` with NO diff to review,
#    because it is never added. Nothing matches today. Trade-off routed to #45; anchoring locally
#    would recreate the divergence HIGH 3 objected to.
#
# Why this file exists at all: the repo had no .gitignore, so Python bytecode from scripts/
# appeared as untracked noise in every `git status` — which is how humans and agents judge
# whether a tree is clean before starting work (#304).
#
# Scope note: per GOV-STANDARD-008 §6.1 (item 3), the SSoT linter MUST respect .gitignore and
# treats anything matching it as OUT OF SCOPE for validation. Adding a pattern here is therefore
# a governance change, not housekeeping. (Note that standard scopes the linter's caller workflow
# to "every other studio repository", and nothing currently running in THIS repo reads .gitignore
# — so the de-scoping is prospective here, not yet operative.)
#
# Verified: no currently-tracked file matches any pattern —
#   git ls-files | git check-ignore --no-index --stdin     → empty, exit 1, across 341 files
# The --no-index is REQUIRED and not optional: without it, check-ignore consults the index and
# never reports a tracked path, so the pipeline returns empty for ANY .gitignore, including `*`.
# The earlier form of this line omitted it and was therefore a test that could not fail.

# Gencraft Studio - Standard .gitignore (v1.0)
# This file is part of gct-repo-template-standard and should be the base for all new repositories.

# Node.js
# Dependencies are managed by package managers, do not commit them.
node_modules/
# Build output
dist/
build/
# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo
# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#  before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Unit test / coverage reports
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.py,cover
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/

# Translations
*.mo
*.pot

# Django stuff:
*.log
local_settings.py
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal

# Flask stuff:
instance/
.webassets-cache

# Scrapy stuff:
.scrapy

# Sphinx documentation
docs/_build/

# PyBuilder
target/

# Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints

# IPython
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to consider not ignoring
#   .python-version, since it is useful for users to know what version
#   of python is required.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock
#   in version control. But in case you prefer not to, then here is a line:
# Pipfile.lock

# PEP 582; __pypackages__ directory
__pypackages__/

# Celery stuff
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# SageMath parsed files
*.sage.py

# Environments
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Spyder project settings
.spyderproject
.spyproject

# Rope project settings
.ropeproject

# mkdocs documentation
/site

# mypy
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# Pyre type checker
.pyre/

# pytype static analyzer
.pytype/

# Cython debug symbols
cython_debug/
# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Sensitive Environment Variables
# NEVER commit .env files. Use a .env.example as a template if needed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS & Editor Specific
# macOS
.DS_Store
# Vim
*~
*.swp
# VSCode
.vscode/

# Java (for completeness)
*.class
*.jar

# Local Terraform directories
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# .tfvars files
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Crash log files
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Ignore any .tfplan files
*.tfplan

# Ignore generated override files
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Ignore CLI configuration files
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REPO-SPECIFIC ADDENDUM — additions beyond the canonical template
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep this section minimal; prefer upstreaming genuinely universal patterns to
# gct-repo-template-standard so every repo benefits instead of drifting.

# Windows thumbnail cache — not in the canonical template (upstreamed as
# GenCr-ft/gct-repo-template-standard#45; drop this line once that lands and re-sync)
Thumbs.db
